1
00:00:39,955 --> 00:00:47,805
Hello, North Carolina.
北卡罗来纳州，你们好！

2
00:00:47,815 --> 00:00:53,921
Are we having a good time tonight or what?
今晚大家开心不开心？

3
00:00:56,540 --> 00:01:04,180
North Carolinians, you have made your voices heard and they were loud.
北卡的朋友们，你们发出了自己的声音，而且响亮无比。

4
00:01:06,370 --> 00:01:07,950
Thank you all so much.
非常感谢大家。

5
00:01:08,430 --> 00:01:11,590
There's a few people I need to thank before anybody else.
首先，我要感谢几个人。

6
00:01:12,130 --> 00:01:22,140
To my amazing wife, Kristen, my wonderful daughters, and the rest of my family over here.
我了不起的妻子克里斯汀、出色的女儿们，以及在场的其他家人。

7
00:01:24,159 --> 00:01:27,150
I am so grateful for your love and support.
我无比感激你们的爱与支持。

8
00:01:27,690 --> 00:01:32,530
You guys are the light of my life and I could not do it without you.
你们照亮了我的生命；没有你们，我做不到这一切。

9
00:01:33,563 --> 00:01:47,440
And to everyone here, including our volunteers, staff, and supporters in this campaign, thank you for everything you did to take this United States Senate seat back for the people of North Carolina.
感谢在座每一个人，包括志愿者、工作人员和支持者；你们所做的一切，帮助北卡罗来纳州人民夺回了这个美国参议院席位。

10
00:01:52,280 --> 00:01:59,320
Now, I know this was a hard-fought race, and I do wish God's blessings for Michael Whatley and his family.
我知道这是一场艰苦的竞选，愿上帝保佑迈克尔·沃特利和他的家人。

11
00:01:59,760 --> 00:02:03,700
I spoke with him earlier tonight and he acknowledged our victory.
今晚早些时候，我与他通了话，他承认了我们的胜利。

12
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:11,240
You know, 16 months ago, we launched this campaign together.
十六个月前，我们一起启动了这场竞选。

13
00:02:12,060 --> 00:02:18,140
We knew that for too many people in North Carolina, the middle class was feeling like a distant dream.
我们知道，对太多北卡人来说，跻身中产阶层已像一个遥远的梦想。

14
00:02:18,520 --> 00:02:26,680
We knew that the Washington DC insiders and the richest Americans were getting unimaginable wealth at our expense.
我们知道，华盛顿的内部人士和美国最富有的人，正在以我们的利益为代价，攫取难以想象的财富。

15
00:02:27,420 --> 00:02:32,520
We knew that the chaos and corruption in Washington were hurting our people.
我们知道，华盛顿的混乱和腐败，正在伤害我们的人民。

16
00:02:33,300 --> 00:02:37,180
Today you said this has to stop.
今天，你们说：这一切必须停止。

17
00:02:41,200 --> 00:02:56,840
And as your new United States Senator, I am ready to take that message to Washington and work to do something about it.
作为你们新当选的美国参议员，我已准备好把这句话带到华盛顿，并采取行动。

18
00:03:00,127 --> 00:03:00,983
All right.
好的。

19
00:03:00,983 --> 00:03:01,133
Yeah.
是的。

20
00:03:01,590 --> 00:03:09,490
It would have been easier for us to just complain and watch from the sidelines, to shake our heads and turn away.
我们本可以只在场边抱怨、观望，摇摇头，转身离开；那样更容易。

21
00:03:10,250 --> 00:03:13,530
It would have been easier, but it wouldn't have been right.
那样更容易，却不正确。

22
00:03:15,450 --> 00:03:21,270
And I've told you many times on Sundays in church, I kept coming back to a passage from the book of Luke.
我多次告诉过你们，星期日在教堂里，我总会想起《路加福音》中的一段话。

23
00:03:21,590 --> 00:03:26,090
To whom much is given, much is required.
多给谁，就向谁多取；多托谁，就向谁多要。

24
00:03:28,880 --> 00:03:35,420
And I thought about the many blessings we have in North Carolina that I have in my life.
我想起北卡罗来纳州拥有的种种福分，也想起我人生中的种种福分。

25
00:03:36,100 --> 00:03:45,312
And I knew what was required of me and you knew what was required of us.
我知道自己该承担什么，而你们也知道，我们共同该承担什么。

26
00:03:45,500 --> 00:03:50,640
This campaign was powered by you, the people of North Carolina.
为这场竞选提供力量的，是你们，北卡罗来纳州人民。

27
00:03:51,660 --> 00:03:56,700
And together, we're standing up for the people Washington has let down.
我们一起，为那些被华盛顿辜负的人挺身而出。

28
00:03:59,920 --> 00:04:03,940
The small business owners watching their livelihoods disappear because of tariffs.
为眼看关税摧毁自己生计的小企业主。

29
00:04:04,700 --> 00:04:09,240
The people who need health care and are terrified of seeing the federal government take it away.
为那些需要医疗服务、却害怕联邦政府将其夺走的人。

30
00:04:09,680 --> 00:04:16,280
The farmers getting crushed by the cost of fertilizer and diesel because of this neverending war.
为那些因这场无休止的战争，承受高昂化肥和柴油成本、被压得喘不过气的农民。

31
00:04:16,660 --> 00:04:30,240
The hardworking families and the people on fixed incomes who desperately need their elected officials to recognize how expensive things are and to work to make stuff cost less.
为勤劳的家庭、依靠固定收入生活的人；他们迫切需要民选官员看见物价有多高，采取行动降低开支。

32
00:04:33,880 --> 00:04:40,560
You know, North Carolinians work hard and they shouldn't need a lobbyist to unlock the American dream.
北卡人辛勤工作，他们不该还需要一个说客，才能敲开美国梦的大门。

33
00:04:41,600 --> 00:04:46,240
That should be the job of the people they elect to represent them.
这本该是他们选出的代表应该做的工作。

34
00:04:46,720 --> 00:04:49,760
And North Carolinians, I accept your job offer.
北卡人民，我接受你们的这份工作聘请。

35
00:04:54,800 --> 00:05:03,640
Tonight, guys, we told Washington loud and clear that North Carolinians will always matter more than the billionaires and the insiders.
今晚，我们响亮而明确地告诉华盛顿：北卡人民，永远比亿万富翁和内部权贵更重要。

36
00:05:05,660 --> 00:05:12,380
Tonight, we showed the country that when everyday people come together, we can make change.
今晚，我们向全国证明，普通人团结起来，就能带来改变。

37
00:05:15,620 --> 00:05:20,220
Tonight, we let everyone know that we are just getting started.
今晚，我们让所有人知道，我们才刚刚开始。

38
00:05:23,540 --> 00:05:30,768
Guys, tonight the campaign ends, but tomorrow the work of governing begins.
今晚竞选结束，但明天，治理的工作就开始了。

39
00:05:34,370 --> 00:05:45,290
We have to work to make health care, housing and groceries more affordable to end this war and stop the pain at the pump.
我们必须让医疗、住房和食品更负担得起，结束这场战争，减轻人们在加油站承受的痛苦。

40
00:05:45,290 --> 00:05:48,730
To protect Medicaid expansion.
保护医疗补助扩展政策。

41
00:05:48,730 --> 00:05:58,130
We work so hard for, to stop corruption and take on special interests that get rich while people struggle to get by.
那是我们辛苦争取来的；我们还要制止腐败，挑战那些在人们艰难度日时大发横财的利益集团。

42
00:05:59,430 --> 00:06:04,810
To strengthen our democracy and live up to this nation's highest ideals.
巩固民主，实现这个国家最崇高的理想。

43
00:06:05,950 --> 00:06:09,510
Hey guys, it won't be easy and it won't be simple.
各位，这不会容易，也不会简单。

44
00:06:10,030 --> 00:06:15,750
But I know that to whom much is given, much is required.
但我知道：受托越多，责任越大。

45
00:06:16,930 --> 00:06:21,850
Guys, in North Carolina, we don't just believe in the promise of tomorrow.
在北卡，我们不只是相信明天的希望。

46
00:06:22,430 --> 00:06:23,310
We become it.
我们让希望成为现实。

47
00:06:23,310 --> 00:06:32,690
First in flight, first colony to demand independence, first public university.
率先实现飞行、率先提出独立要求的殖民地、第一所公立大学。

48
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:44,020
We race to lead because we know what hope the future holds.
我们争当先行者，因为我们知道，未来蕴藏着怎样的希望。

49
00:06:44,480 --> 00:06:51,600
And when you've got hope, when you've got hope, anything is possible.
而只要心怀希望，一切皆有可能。

50
00:06:55,180 --> 00:07:03,700
Tonight, guys, I am deeply grateful for and humbled by the confidence and trust you have once again placed in me.
今晚，对于你们再次给予我的信心与信任，我深怀感激，也倍感谦卑。

51
00:07:03,900 --> 00:07:20,320
I am determined that no matter the challenges that confront me, I will be an independent voice ready to work with anyone to do what's right for this amazing state that has given me so much.
无论面对什么挑战，我都会坚持独立发声，与任何愿意为这个给予我如此之多的伟大州做正确事情的人合作。

52
00:07:20,600 --> 00:07:24,160
Guys, I will be your voice.
各位，我会替你们发声。

53
00:07:25,660 --> 00:07:30,520
As your senator, I will always put you, the people of North Carolina, first.
作为你们的参议员，我始终会把北卡罗来纳州人民放在第一位。

54
00:07:31,380 --> 00:07:33,300
I will put you before politics.
把你们放在政治算计之前。

55
00:07:33,751 --> 00:07:35,540
I'll put you before party.
放在党派之前。

56
00:07:36,140 --> 00:07:37,920
I will put you before power.
放在权力之前。

57
00:07:38,300 --> 00:07:41,180
I'm not going to Washington to be something.
我去华盛顿，不是为了当什么大人物。

58
00:07:41,919 --> 00:07:45,045
I'm going to Washington to do something.
而是为了真正做些事情。

59
00:07:52,319 --> 00:07:56,711
And at the end of the day, I am still a prisoner of hope.
归根结底，我仍是一个始终被希望牢牢牵引的人。

60
00:07:57,350 --> 00:08:01,170
I truly believe that our best days lie ahead.
我真心相信，我们最好的日子还在前方。

61
00:08:01,810 --> 00:08:07,310
That we can make the course correction that our great country so badly needs.
相信我们能为这个伟大的国家，作出它如此迫切需要的方向修正。

62
00:08:08,310 --> 00:08:14,342
That North Carolina and the United States have a future teeming with possibilities.
相信北卡罗来纳州和美国，都拥有充满可能性的未来。

63
00:08:14,870 --> 00:08:17,567
So, what do you say, North Carolina?
北卡的朋友们，你们怎么说？

64
00:08:22,330 --> 00:08:23,790
Are you ready for change?
你们准备好迎接改变了吗？

65
00:08:26,950 --> 00:08:30,070
Are you ready to turn things around for hardworking people?
准备好为辛勤工作的人民扭转局面了吗？

66
00:08:32,380 --> 00:08:35,200
Are you ready to meet the promise of tomorrow?
准备好实现明天的希望了吗？

67
00:08:37,190 --> 00:08:38,390
I am too.
我也准备好了。

68
00:08:39,050 --> 00:08:44,010
May God bless all of you, our country, and the great state of North Carolina.
愿上帝保佑各位，保佑我们的国家，保佑伟大的北卡罗来纳州。

69
00:08:44,450 --> 00:08:45,650
Thank you very much.
非常感谢。

70
00:08:47,040 --> 00:08:49,236
Thank you.
谢谢。